{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines","id":1190520,"title":"[2E] Solo Focused CoD gamelines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-28T18:41:51-08:00","id":1190520,"title":"[2E] Solo Focused CoD gamelines","content":"So there is subtopic discussion of mine in <b>Beast: The Primordial </b>forum I think is showing much boarder problem some STs have with few of CoD games. Nominally, it's that some of those games are written as for Solo Games - 1 on 1 player and ST sessions - in mind more than group activity. Will focus here on 2E versions of gamelines, for having more clear picture, as some of them were under big rewrite. Here are my and <b>Wormwood</b>'s points on this topic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190274#post1190274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, it's a problem with <b>Beast: The Primodial</b> me and few other STs I talked to have. It's all about 'my Beast', not the group at large - ironically to Family theme of the game. Werewolves hunt together in packs. Mages uncover mystical secret in cabals. Even vampires are doing their politics by pulling coteries resources together. In <b>Beast</b> you sate YOUR OWN Hunger. YOU are aiming to become Apex. Go YOURSELF for Inheritance. All those actions are done by ONE PC, not whole group. <b>BtP</b>, like <b>Promethean the Created</b>, seems to be made for solo games - the 'snowflake issue' - and this is problem for many STs wanting to run it as multi-players group. It's a MUCH less problem than <b>PtC</b> - but it's there. So this is why I need Chronicles Seeds - to see <i>possibility</i> for chronicle for few PCs as one story in <b>BtP</b> - not collection of solo games mixed together.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1189434-begotten-of-the-past?p=1190337#post1190337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I grant you that Werewolves have a very special bond as a Pack In-Setting. But Mages uncover mystical secrets in Cabals because they cannot do it by themselves, or a majority (In-setting) would. Coteries, likewise, break apart once they don't need each other anymore. Demon Rings (?) are more of an uneasy truce than anything else. Changelings and Hunters at least share similar traumata, but the idea of &quot;you have come together as people who went through the same supernatural event&quot; is the basic premise of the whole gig.<br /> A special bond that is shared by the members <i>beyond </i>that basic premise IMO only applies to Werewolf, Promethean and Beast. As a Werewolf player, I don't need to tell you about werewolves. Prometheans are united by a common goal, the desire to keep each other in check and on the right path, mitigate inherent drawbacks of their existance and <i>metaphysically bind themselves to each other</i>. Beasts see below.<br /> Regarding the 'Sate YOUR HUNGER': same is true for every other splat. Vampires sate their hunger, not their friends'. You cannot eat for a friend. Even the 'hunting as a Pack' thing is a desire of singular werewolves.<br /> <br /> I don't think Beast is made for Solo-Adventures (nor do I think Promethean is) - they work solo, yes, but so do most splats. However, they <i>shine </i>with a small group. Also, &quot;Snowflaking&quot; is more of a problem with Z-Splats etc, when people need to be &quot;the only/first/last of their kind&quot;, feel the need to be more rare and powerful/useful/special than their fellow players or otherwise cannot be satisfied with a 'normal' template to breath life into. Beasts are merely quite customizable (though, at least mechanically, not to the same degree as Changelings and Demons). Not bashing z-splats here - I love them, they can add a great layer of meaning or depth to a character, but shouldn't completely define the character.<br /> Futhermore, the moment you play a one-person-game, (and as I said, that works JUST as well with every other splat as it does with Beast, with the possible exception of W:tF, imo) everything becomes 'Special Snowflake-y' very quickly (unless you specifically grognard it VtM style): Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Demon, Beast, Mummy, Hunter, Geist - doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Some more points on Beasts being about &quot;My Beast&quot;:<br /> - One way of sating a Beast's Hunger is, literally, to help their Family members feed themselves (help Mages hunt for Artifacts, participate in a Siskur-Dah, help a Changeling get that Glamour...). This comes especially in handy for those Beasts that take issue with their Horror's Hunger. That is plenty of incentive to not work alone, and even go out of your way to help others. There is even similarity to how Uratha accept other Supernaturals if they help them Hunt - there is a purpose to the action, and usually mutually beneficial.<br /> - One major way of expanding their Lair (a.k.a. grow as a Monster/person) is to seek out places where your supernatural relatives left a lasting impression. The more the Beast learns about what took place, the more people and supernaturals involved they meet, the better their chances of finding and claiming a chamber. This is a very strong incentive to learn more about the occult history of the area, get to know the local things that go bump in the night (not just splats, but also horrors, classic antagonists, ghosts, spirits, whatever - the more you get to know, the better!). This is even mechanically encouraged by giving the same amount of dice for being the supernatural that caused the impact in question and having encountered the supernatural in question (+3). Even more dice are given if the Beast has Family Ties with this supernatural being (+5!).<br /> - Broodmates can draw on each other's Lair Traits to call down their own - literally exponentially making them stronger than lone wolves; a very literal &quot;Power of Friendship&quot;. The Mother's Kiss even underlines this by giving Beasts a Mentor-Stance - the more powerful a Beast, the better it can support WEAKER Family members. This makes the most sense if both have a different focus and thus compliment each other. Furthermore, being strongly acquainted with certain splat grants you access to new powers: Nightmares are literally reflections of how other supernaturals (or even specific individuals) spread Fear - a Beast looking to increase its toolset needs to interact meaningfully with other supernaturals.<br /> - Like all the other splats, Beasts have unique antagonists trying to hunt them down - unlike in most other cases, though, their enemies get special powers that only work against the Children - plenty of incentive to try and invite other supernaturals into their Brood, to better defend themselves.<br /> - &quot;Go YOURSELF for Inheritance&quot;. Well, first of all 2 out of 3 Inheritances are more like alternate game-overs/suicides than winning. Next, a Beast going for an Inheritance is very similar to a Mage going for Archmage. That is also one Mage going for it, not a whole Cabal having the goal of making that one dude Archmage. And if you say &quot;well, they can support him and he relies on them&quot; - well, duh, <i>same for Broods</i>.<br /> - Beasts get nice little set-ups to pretend to be part of another splat. This is to encourage IC exploration of other supernatural societies. Plenty of story-hooks here: Beast new in town, follows the first vamp into their society, becomes friends and boom, fudges up and their cover is blown. How will their alleged 'friends' react? Or: Beast went undercover in a Cabal for some time, but cannot keep lying to their Family any longer. But they might decide it makes a more interesting test subject than friend, or consider it a threat. On the other hand, they might welcome the options the Beast brings to the table. But then how will others react to them indulging a 'pet'? etc etc.<br /> - Not every Beast wants to be Apex, same as not every Kindred wants to be Prince. It's<i> An</i> endgame, not the only one. Plus Broods might like to have the Apex in their Brood, because it would give THEM ALL quite the substantial powerboost (one of our Lair Traits is in EVERY Chamber? AWESOME! LET'S DO IT!). So they might actually work together to make one amongst them Apex.<br /> - Core literally states that most Beasts have an inherent desire for companionship and do not want to be left to their own devices. That isn't too tough to roleplay, imo.<br /> - Beasts need to act physically, but also mentally and socially. They have the same needs as all other splats to cover the Heroic Groups basis (Be that Tank, Brawler, Smart Guy, Silver Tongue, Thief or whatever other template you want to use).<br /> And, most importantly imo for non-mechanical reasons:<br /> - Broods <i>literally </i>connect their 'Souls' and can take a hike in each other's soul. They even invite their Cousin Broodmates into their 'Souls'. You think this sort of connection will be as haphazard and instable as most Coteries? On the other hand, you doubt it would be as strong as a Promethean Branded Throng or Werewolf Pack?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the things you mentioned don't make sense to me. You see lack of focus; I see wealth of opportunities. You see &quot;Hunting together&quot; in Werewolf, but don't see &quot;Family&quot; in Beast?<br /> The way I see it, a Werewolf grows strong alone, to work primarily as part of a Pack - a Beast might (<i>might!</i> not does!) work alone, but mostly grows <i>thanks to others</i>.<br /> I don't see how that is, at all, problematic. Different, sure. It's supposed to be, it's a different gameline.<br /> Maybe it's just not your cup of tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:14:35-08:00","id":1190528,"title":"","content":"Now, my answering point's risen by <b>Wormwood</b>.<br /> <br /> 1. There is very pressing narrative force in Mage to form cabals - i.e. other mages will get's the secrets you cannot get yourself. Not only this that stat starting mages are VERY weak and easily to be eaten by other supernatural forces of CoD universe. The only real narrative force for Beasts to connect is oppression from Heroes - and even this seems a bit stretch without some very powerful antagonistic individuals. About coteries in Vampire and circles in Demon - maybe I do not run this as games because of this in build selfishness? Maybe. Promethean is THE MOST 'My PC' game in CoD pond - it's whole reason to be is 'my character wants to be human - IN THIS WAY'. If character goals clashes, it's very little narrative force for them to be together - ST need to extensively sew Milestones for each PC to depend on other players only to said to first player \u2018no, you did not marked Milestone with this awesome action \u2013 you need more of it\u2026 Or maybe other one for working on it\u2026\u2019. Changelings and especially Hunters are really good on narrative forcing players to cooperate - in Changeling you have whole aspect of 'you come from the same strange insane realm of torture together' ( shared PTSD, in reality ). And hunters are all about 'we MUST cooperate to survive the night, or the monster will kill us'. I do not feel the same in Beast - it's basically 'I like you guys, but...' - and there is then start of solo scenes like Hunger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which leads us to...<br /> <br /> 2. Hungers in Beast are VERY different. In Vampire - all PCs are craving blood. So joined scenes of hunting can be made. Even if not - seeking blood is very simple to devise on foot - so ST derail time for each PC on session is very little. Hunting in Werewolf is shared from logical reasons, it's a premise of game in fact. Getting Mana in Mage is complicated thing - but's there other PCs shine in a way 'we can make it work together'. Changeling works more or less the same as Vampire - as emotions are 'getting extra' for doing slightly more specific way of gathering, but whole motley can feed from the same powerful emotional scene. Promethean is once again \u2018it\u2019s my way of getting Pyros\u2019 here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3. Points risen on the Beasts, as counterarguments \u2013 I will ponder on them more. Sounds a bit more convincing to work in game. But best would be to point where in rules of <b>BtP</b> core there is intensification of collaboration on Begotten groups parts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T05:57:04-08:00","id":1190630,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but does this really need its own thread, Wyrd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:14:00-08:00","id":1190649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1190630#post1190630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but does this really need its own thread, Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does if Wyrd feels like it does <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's better than derailing the existing topic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:07:40-08:00","id":1191095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1190528#post1190528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, my answering point's risen by <b>Wormwood</b>.<br /> <br /> 1. There is very pressing narrative force in Mage to form cabals - i.e. other mages will get's the secrets you cannot get yourself. Not only this that stat starting mages are VERY weak and easily to be eaten by other supernatural forces of CoD universe. The only real narrative force for Beasts to connect is oppression from Heroes - and even this seems a bit stretch without some very powerful antagonistic individuals. About coteries in Vampire and circles in Demon - maybe I do not run this as games because of this in build selfishness? Maybe. Promethean is THE MOST 'My PC' game in CoD pond - it's whole reason to be is 'my character wants to be human - IN THIS WAY'. If character goals clashes, it's very little narrative force for them to be together - ST need to extensively sew Milestones for each PC to depend on other players only to said to first player \u2018no, you did not marked Milestone with this awesome action \u2013 you need more of it\u2026 Or maybe other one for working on it\u2026\u2019. Changelings and especially Hunters are really good on narrative forcing players to cooperate - in Changeling you have whole aspect of 'you come from the same strange insane realm of torture together' ( shared PTSD, in reality ). And hunters are all about 'we MUST cooperate to survive the night, or the monster will kill us'. I do not feel the same in Beast - it's basically 'I like you guys, but...' - and there is then start of solo scenes like Hunger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which leads us to...<br /> <br /> 2. Hungers in Beast are VERY different. In Vampire - all PCs are craving blood. So joined scenes of hunting can be made. Even if not - seeking blood is very simple to devise on foot - so ST derail time for each PC on session is very little. Hunting in Werewolf is shared from logical reasons, it's a premise of game in fact. Getting Mana in Mage is complicated thing - but's there other PCs shine in a way 'we can make it work together'. Changeling works more or less the same as Vampire - as emotions are 'getting extra' for doing slightly more specific way of gathering, but whole motley can feed from the same powerful emotional scene. Promethean is once again \u2018it\u2019s my way of getting Pyros\u2019 here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3. Points risen on the Beasts, as counterarguments \u2013 I will ponder on them more. Sounds a bit more convincing to work in game. But best would be to point where in rules of <b>BtP</b> core there is intensification of collaboration on Begotten groups parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The narrative Force that connects Beasts is their desire for company, their extreme sense of Family, and the fact they fit in well with almost every supernatural denizen of the ChroD. Having your soul replaced by a monster when another nightmare 'ate' yours is similarly connecting as your examples, imo. Especially if there is the feeling of &quot;hey, those are Siblings!&quot; involved.<br /> Your description of Promethean does not mirror my experience of playing it in the slightest. Few games I've played were that focused on each player's char trying to work together, seamlessly coming together. So yeah, our reading, understanding and experience of these games simply differs in the most elementary aspects.<br /> <br /> 2. And a whole Brood can feed by watching either of their members feed, which is something Beasts would make extreme use of, because you don't want to waste opportunities like that. I consider the fact that Beasts have different Hungers a boon of the gameline, and love the diversity. Still, all Beasts are united in the fact that they need to spread Fear to Feed. You can also use less time on derailing the game by having a different focus and simply spending less time on the feeding, if that's your cup of tea. But to me, it is one of the bits that seperates it from playing &quot;Friendly Neighbourhood Supernaturals&quot;. Again, fundamentally different reading, understanding, interpretation and experiences.<br /> <br /> 3. I do not know what you want, mechanical points? Nor do I think there needs to be an explicit statement that says so, but maybe you were asking for something like this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever the supernatural scene in a region, the Children usually build close ties with other local Beasts, forming a group known as a brood. Members of a brood weave their Lairs together to forge a stronger shared realm, which in turn allows them a greater degree of security against outside threats such as Heroes. Sating one\u2019s Hunger is also easier with a brood, as the group can collectively derive sustenance when one member feeds. </div> </div> </div> or <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The human need for companionship never goes away, even when humanity does. If anything, a Beast feels its loss more keenly. The Devouring opens the door to a Family the Beast never even knew he had. They accept him for what he is, no questions asked, and stand by him when the Hero comes to shed his blood </div> </div> </div> or <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts band together for the same reasons humans do: camaraderie, convenience, and mutual protection. They lack the world-spanning secret societies of mages and vampires, but the bonds they share are far more intimate. Indeed, the brood is Beast society as far as its members are concerned. Each is a surrogate family with its own territory defined by their collective influence on the Primordial Dream and how many people they affect. A brood can host any combination, not just Family members. Even other creatures, such as vampires and werewolves, are welcome to join. Beasts are a clannish lot. They help their kin when possible \u2014 and convenient \u2014 but nothing compares to the bond between broodmates. They cling to each other and jealously guard their territory against outsiders. </div> </div> </div><br /> I think our opinions are simply to different, and we simply will have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:27:19-08:00","id":1191206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191095#post1191095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The narrative Force that connects Beasts is their desire for company, their extreme sense of Family, and the fact they fit in well with almost every supernatural denizen of the ChroD. Having your soul replaced by a monster when another nightmare 'ate' yours is similarly connecting as your examples, imo. Especially if there is the feeling of &quot;hey, those are Siblings!&quot; involved.<br /> Your description of Promethean does not mirror my experience of playing it in the slightest. Few games I've played were that focused on each player's char trying to work together, seamlessly coming together. So yeah, our reading, understanding and experience of these games simply differs in the most elementary aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You come from the view that players are 'nice' too one another, even go lenghts after one another. My gameplay experiance is that players thinks in general for what's good for <i>their</i> characters. Sure, they can work together if it's beneficial to both parties - but onces nicties pass, they try to pull narrative in each ones course. The typical 'I don't like you guys now' is most extreme version of it, there are a lot of 'plot backstabing' that are less obvious inside game session. <b><i>Narrative Force</i></b> in chronicle I talk here about is exactly to prevent from this spliting of groups main ideas on plot. Free roaming Begotten and Created in this take are problem - unless you have very good Narrative Force for cooperation in-build in chronicle - if there is little in gameline itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191095#post1191095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. And a whole Brood can feed by watching either of their members feed, which is something Beasts would make extreme use of, because you don't want to waste opportunities like that. I consider the fact that Beasts have different Hungers a boon of the gameline, and love the diversity. Still, all Beasts are united in the fact that they need to spread Fear to Feed. You can also use less time on derailing the game by having a different focus and simply spending less time on the feeding, if that's your cup of tea. But to me, it is one of the bits that seperates it from playing &quot;Friendly Neighbourhood Supernaturals&quot;. Again, fundamentally different reading, understanding, interpretation and experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, if Beasts can use Family Dinner on one another - it's <i>much</i> less problem I thought it was on passing reading the corebook I had.<br /> <b>Still, how much Family Dinner is for other Beasts than Main Eater?</b> If they can get as much Satiety as him, one point less - or is it like Main Eater get's 4 and rest of Brood can only get's 1?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191095#post1191095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I do not know what you want, mechanical points? Nor do I think there needs to be an explicit statement that says so, but maybe you were asking for something like this:</div> </div> </div> </div>More points from gameline mechanics, not the fluff saying 'we need to be nice to one another'. Cause, from my ST experience, when tension in player groups rises - it's not sentiment that makes it stay together. Just common interests - based on common environment advantages - that comes from mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T20:54:49-08:00","id":1191223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191206#post1191206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, if Beasts can use Family Dinner on one another - it's <i>much</i> less problem I thought it was on passing reading the corebook I had.<br /> <b>Still, how much Family Dinner is for other Beasts than Main Eater?</b> If they can get as much Satiety as him, one point less - or is it like Main Eater get's 4 and rest of Brood can only get's 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>It functions like a normal family dinner, how much the &quot;main eater&quot; gets is irrelevant to the amount other beasts get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:30:06-08:00","id":1191235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191206#post1191206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You come from the view that players are 'nice' too one another, even go lenghts after one another. My gameplay experiance is that players thinks in general for what's good for <i>their</i> characters. Sure, they can work together if it's beneficial to both parties - but onces nicties pass, they try to pull narrative in each ones course. The typical 'I don't like you guys now' is most extreme version of it, there are a lot of 'plot backstabing' that are less obvious inside game session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hamster, I'm gonna go out on a limb here and suggest that the problem here is the players, not the game. If someone can't handle cooperation and sharing, they either need to go back to kindergarten or stick to one-on-one play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:37:27-08:00","id":1191237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191223#post1191223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It functions like a normal family dinner, how much the &quot;main eater&quot; gets is irrelevant to the amount other beasts get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the rules on Family Dinner - So all the other Brood members must to do is only to watch their 'close friend' Begotten? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well, it's sub-optimal, as 'Main Eater' needs to do all the Hunger hunting and rest of Brood just watch. Okay, there is the thing if Main Eater 'human side' do not accept what her Horror needs her to do - and other Brood members helps to solve conundrum - but it's still 'you make all the job done, we will sit and watch'.<br /> <br /> Also - question more related to Beast as game, but related to this thread - <b>Can Begotten sate their Hunger on other Beasts? ( Or other supernaturals for that matter? ) </b>I always thought you need to target humans to sate Horrors Hunger.<br /> <br /> If Broodmate A can sate his Hunger on willing Broodmate B - it solved most dire problem I have with Beast: The Primordial as game. It's a bit sick idea - when monster feed on fear of other monster - but from ST perspective it's highten tense scene between two PCs that rest of Brood can benefit by interacting also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:45:03-08:00","id":1191241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191235#post1191235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hamster, I'm gonna go out on a limb here and suggest that the problem here is the players, not the game. If someone can't handle cooperation and sharing, they either need to go back to kindergarten or stick to one-on-one play.</div> </div> </div> </div>You play with people you have. And those things 'goes out in practice' - i.e. in gameplay - not on starting on game. <b>In my 16 years of game mastering various games and groups I <i>never</i> heard once before game 'I'm selfish player, not liking to cooperate with others' to just move them from start of particular games I run.</b> Still, this people have <i>subconscious</i> tendency to play that way - they are not even aware about this. Even when those players are great in other domains and generally - outside cooperation - are really good to the plot and roleplaying of the group. <b>Soooo it's better to have Narrative Force in the chronicle as one of the good players of yours uncover to be not so cooperating with other players. Just in case. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T22:15:14-08:00","id":1191251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191241#post1191241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You play with people you have. And those things 'goes out in practice' - i.e. in gameplay - not on starting on game. <b>In my 16 years of game mastering various games and groups I <i>never</i> heard once before game 'I'm selfish player, not liking to cooperate with others' to just move them from start of particular games I run.</b> Still, this people have <i>subconscious</i> tendency to play that way - they are not even aware about this. Even when those players are great in other domains and generally - outside cooperation - are really good to the plot and roleplaying of the group. <b>Soooo it's better to have Narrative Force in the chronicle as one of the good players of yours uncover to be not so cooperating with other players. Just in case. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's called having players who are the problem, and it is not a universal problem.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, it's called having a half-measure for players who are problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T03:20:40-08:00","id":1191296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191206#post1191206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You come from the view that players are 'nice' too one another, even go lenghts after one another. My gameplay experiance is that players thinks in general for what's good for <i>their</i> characters. Sure, they can work together if it's beneficial to both parties - but onces nicties pass, they try to pull narrative in each ones course. The typical 'I don't like you guys now' is most extreme version of it, there are a lot of 'plot backstabing' that are less obvious inside game session. <b><i>Narrative Force</i></b> in chronicle I talk here about is exactly to prevent from this spliting of groups main ideas on plot. Free roaming Begotten and Created in this take are problem - unless you have very good Narrative Force for cooperation in-build in chronicle - if there is little in gameline itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not my &quot;point of view&quot;, it's my experience. I can only be sorry that it differs so much from yours. Never needed this &quot;Narrative Force&quot;, people simply properly RP'ed and worked together.<br /> If nothing else, this sounds like they were too similar in their specialization to me. After all, every player should get a chance to shine during a chronicle (if not each chapter). If that is not the case, chars and plot are not a good fit imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191206#post1191206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, if Beasts can use Family Dinner on one another - it's <i>much</i> less problem I thought it was on passing reading the corebook I had.<br /> <b>Still, how much Family Dinner is for other Beasts than Main Eater?</b> If they can get as much Satiety as him, one point less - or is it like Main Eater get's 4 and rest of Brood can only get's 1?</div> </div> </div> </div> and <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Read the rules on Family Dinner - So all the other Brood members must to do is only to watch their 'close friend' Begotten? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Well, it's sub-optimal, as 'Main Eater' needs to do all the Hunger hunting and rest of Brood just watch. Okay, there is the thing if Main Eater 'human side' do not accept what her Horror needs her to do - and other Brood members helps to solve conundrum - but it's still 'you make all the job done, we will sit and watch'.<br /> <br /> Also - question more related to Beast as game, but related to this thread - <b>Can Begotten sate their Hunger on other Beasts? ( Or other supernaturals for that matter? ) </b>I always thought you need to target humans to sate Horrors Hunger.<br /> <br /> If Broodmate A can sate his Hunger on willing Broodmate B - it solved most dire problem I have with Beast: The Primordial as game. It's a bit sick idea - when monster feed on fear of other monster - but from ST perspective it's highten tense scene between two PCs that rest of Brood can benefit by interacting also. </div> </div> </div>Hamster, I will be honest here: I get the feeling you didn't really read the book, which makes a lot of this a bit pointless, and puts the majority of your critic up to now into a bad light - my personal opinion.<br /> Family Dinner yields up to 3 Satiety. The prey must NOT be willing, otherwise it doesn't work. A Beast watching a Mage successfully restore Mana may count for Family Dinner just as much as a Siskur Dah or a Vampire Feeding. Obviously, if another Beast Feeds, that counts, too. This way, a whole Brood may gain 1-3 Satiety for watching one member get their 'fix', even if they get only one Satiety.<br /> Sure, just watching is enough, but decreases the chances of it being successful. One of the short stories in Core described a Vampire feeding under the Protection of a Beast's Darkness Lair Trait.<br /> Supporting the hunter with Mother's Kiss, Lair Traits, Nightmares, Atavisms etc. means a much higher chance of getting Satiety. Group Effort &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; we watch you do your thing.<br /> There is absolutely 0 reason that a Brood or Players should wait while you do your Feeding scene. Instead, people should follow their NATURAL INSTINCT on working together. Why do you think Beasts have an ability that does nothing but support another Supernaturals next supernatural action? This way, Mr. Tanky Bodyguard can support your Daeva in seducing, despite being socially inept and not having any other way to support this action. NOT making use of this ability simply means sabotaging your team and thus yourself.<br /> <br /> And yes, Begotten can Feed on other Supernaturals, Beasts included. However, targets mustn't be willing, or there's no Lesson learned nor the proper amount of Fear involved. You <i>might</i> find a way around this with something like a Horror House or something, were the victims are technically willing, but still capable of experiencing the amount of Shock and Fear needed to sate the Horror's Hunger, but that is a topic that may be cleared up with the Player's guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1191206#post1191206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More points from gameline mechanics, not the fluff saying 'we need to be nice to one another'. Cause, from my ST experience, when tension in player groups rises - it's not sentiment that makes it stay together. Just common interests - based on common environment advantages - that comes from mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can't help you there, never had that trouble with tension in player groups, so not entirely sure what mechanics would prove necessary. To be frank, don't see the mechanical side in werewolf, but then, I don't claim to be knowledgeable about WtF 2ed, since I've never played it nor finished the book. I certainly don't see a mechanical reason for Motleys in Changeling 1ed that is in any way shape or form stronger than the one's presented in Beast.<br /> Can only repeat the mechanics I already pointed out: Mother's Kiss, Family Dinner, Lair Traits. The last of which is a huge boon.<br /> In a Brood of 4 Lair 1 Beasts, each can use four different Lair Traits to call down their own and makes travelling via Primordeal Pathways a lot easier (existing Lair Traits make opening the Pathway easier due to a +1 modifier for each Lair trait). The other Beasts don't even have to be present, but to show how much of a difference that is: 4 lone Beasts vs a Brood of 4 Beasts try to use Lair traits to fight. The very moment at least one Lair Trait is active, the Brood may impose one Lair trait each (Lair 1 limit). The lone Beasts each have to set up the area so that they can call down a Lair Trait, or hope one of the others calls down one of theirs. Worst Case for the lone Beasts, it's 0 Lair Traits vs. 5 (the initial + 1 per Beast). A very significant advantage, considering that spending 1 WP makes your friends immune to the Lair trait. You can be a group of more powerful monsters, I don't care, you will still lose while fighting in a Burning Hurricane while suffering from Toxic poison, having trouble to see through the Downpour while struggling with the Slick ground against the group of otherwise unimpressive enemies who however are unaffected by these things and can freely see, shoot and move.<br /> Mother's Kiss makes physical-oriented chars useful as supporters for social and mental stuff when supernatural abilities are thrown around, and likewise make the 'Face' or 'Brains' of the group very useful by buffing the group's fighter's abilities. This is doubly the case for non-Beasts, because Family Ties adds three dice to the roll.<br /> Family Dinner see above.<br /> <br /> That's all from my side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-03-2018, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T03:37:56-07:00","id":1196433,"title":"","content":"It looks like Mage is also having some large <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1196390-mage-2e-signs-of-sorcery-problem-no-sharing-paths-mage-sight-between-cabal\">'solo focused' problems in gameplay experience</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T08:33:16-07:00","id":1196496,"title":"","content":"Again, after reading through that thread, I have to say I heavily disagree with your point of view, Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Giving one player a spot to shine is <b>absolutely </b>fine - just make sure <b>everyone </b>gets the same treatment once in a while. Hell, I don't see how you can do things any other way, since a chronicle featuring a brawny, a brainy and a pretty PC <i>will </i>need them to act in their relative spheres of competence, or else the other players' concepts and the story won't fit, rendering them useless.<br /> (Tell a story about manipulation and intrigue, influence and the absolute need for secrecy, and see how your social attributes 2/2/2 fighter without subterfuge, persuasion or empathy will fare. Make the story a action-filled martial-arts-war-flick, and see how useful your Intelligence 4 Wits 2 Resolve 2 guy without any Brawl, Athletics, Firearms or Weaponry will be.)<br /> <br /> To go back to that &quot;hacker hacking&quot; analogue that was raised in the thread: if the brainy hacker's hacking, your socialite can still be the one to get the necessary access codes via social engineering (giving the hacker admin priviliges or similar, so make that a +4 on rolls or consider it building equipment, or even make this the basic premise to even be able to attempt to hack), the stealthmaster can still open the doors to get the hacker to the computer best suited (hey, just make it an independent system that cannot be accessed from outside...) and the brute force guy knocks out security guards on the other side of the building to create a diversion. There you go: team effort, everyone gets their chance to shine, all contribute to the same effort by doing what they do best.<br /> Not everyone, and certainly not every PC, needs to be interested in the same things. Those deviations from the normal route caused by explicilty just one character's needs can end up immensely enjoyable due to a variety of reasons, not least of all the fact that the majority of the troupe will find themselves outside their comfort zone, so they will become more creative: I cannot punch the computer into submission. I cannot hack. I CAN, however, keep people away from our hacker. By punching. I contribute to the team effort <i>despite the actual task being out of my waters.</i> So satisfying. Or: I cannot charm a computer. I can try to charm someone to do the job for me, though. I can get codes, keys, access to rooms. By doing what I do best, I get <i>to support my group by making this possible</i>.<br /> <br /> Play with the players' expectations, by turning things around: maybe the hacker doesn't manage to hack the system - It was a trap all along! You need to escape. Computers are now the enemy, so punching boy gets to break them, and stealthy mcthief causes a shortcut in the system after being told by Brainy O'Smarty where to look.<br /> <br /> <br /> Same applies to Mage's mysteries, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T09:11:05-07:00","id":1196507,"title":"","content":"Why <i>should</i> I need to obtain Imbued Item for the most basic games plot to work in cabal, in the first place? CoD games are <i>groups</i> storytelling games, don't they. Let's see...<br /> <br /> Do I need special items to make Sacred Hunt in <b>Werewolf</b>? No, just a Rite that <i>any</i> ( Uratha ) character can have from the start - for 'free'.<br /> <br /> Do I need special items for <b>Beast</b> broods to explore Chambers in Dream? No, they just do it collectively - for <b>free</b>.<br /> <br /> Do I need special powers in <b>Promethean</b> to share alchemical powers and help one another in Pilgrimage? No, they just make Alchemical Pact. ( Items just makes it better, slight. )<br /> <br /> <b>You see here? From what I see, 2E gamelines <i>helps</i> do it's 'Game Main Groups Activity' to share between player characters. </b><br /> <br /> Only Awakened in 2E cannot share the Mage Sight and we end with running 5 different 1on1's in typical group - or have only one character access on general to ones Supernal Realm related Mysteries, like with Aedes example. WHY it need to be this way? Other games simply let you simply share 'Game Main Groups Activity'. In <b>Mage</b> 2E you do some weird and totally unnecessary hacks to let it work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T09:17:36-07:00","id":1196509,"title":"","content":"You cannot 'talk beside' Mystery Scrutiny. You cannot 'go to the mob boss to attack your common enemy' where you having Mystery in Pandemonium. YOU NEED to be able to perceive Pandemonium to be able react with it.<br /> <br /> Splitting actions between players can work with mortals ( or even other supernaturals ), but when we have Supernal Mystery - that are LARGE part of <b>Mage</b> - of one kind - only one player can perceive them.<br /> <br /> And no, using Mind 4 to send the image of what you see to other players is the same 'solution' as using Prime 4 to cast <i>Apocalypse</i> on those around them. I.E. It's <i>not solution</i> for any <b>Mage </b>starting group, as players will not get easily on 4th dot this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T06:53:23-07:00","id":1196780,"title":"","content":"Okay <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, I'll try again.<br /> <br /> There is <i><b>nothing </b></i>inherently wrong with just a Thyrsus being able to perceive the Mystery.<br /> This time, it is a Mystery in Pandemonium, next time, it will be one in Stygia. Everyone gets their time to shine. All's well.<br /> <br /> You can still make it so that you need an Obrimos to get them to the spot from which they can perceive it. You can make it so that the gained knowledge is <i>in code</i>: your Thyrsus can perceive it, yes, but not understand it. Make it a schematic, a map, a crypto-key the group's Mastigos deciphers and copies down. You can make it so that the gained knowledge requires the party's Moros to create a specific perfected material to create the object of the schematic, which could be just a sort of compass leading you to the next mystery, where your Acanthus can open a time-portal to acquire a relic or Grimoir.<br /> <br /> You can make it so that the Mystery within Pandemonium is veiled with Spirit magic - your Mastigos <i>needs</i> the Thyrsus' help taking that down first, despite the latter being unable to see it. However, in an effort of teamwork, he can lend the Mastigos his understanding of Spirit, guiding him much as Tower Control guides the untrained person that takes over the plane as the pilots collapsed for whatever reason. The Thyrsus tries to guide his Cabal mate through symbols and meanings that the latter doesn't understand at all. Let them roll teamwork, at -2 or -3, to give the Scrutinizing Mage a dice bonus. This is hard work, an uphill battle. That makes success all the sweeter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>As long</b> <b>as seeing the Supernal Mystery that only one path can perceive isn't the <u>absolute</u> core or pinnacle of the story, there isn't a single problem with it from my point of view. </b><br /> And since you're the one creating the Mystery in the first place, that should be entirely in your hands.<br /> <br /> And if you don't like it: fine, don't use it. Houserule it that having access to Mind 1 means you can view the Pandemonium Mystery as if you were Mastigos. Houserule it so that with Mind 3, you can share your Mind-Sight with a Themed Cabal.<br /> Ditch what doesn't work for your table. That's always been the golden rule of ChroD.<br /> You're the ST. It's your job to give every player a chance to shine. You control what they can find, what that means, what they need to do to piece together everything to figure out what was hidden. Do that in such a way everyone has a great experience. Everything else is secondary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> RE your claims of Prometheans being simply able to make an Alchemical Pact, I am afraid that is wrong. Only Prometheans on the Path of Lead are capable of Branding a Throng. So yes, you DO need special powers. Or access to someone with those special powers. And Prometheans are rare...<br /> <br /> If every Werewolf can learn the Rite from the beginning, but effectively has to buy it, that doesn't make it free, now does it? It's a 2-dot rite, too. Someone within the group has to give up on a 2-dot Rite so the group can participate in the &quot;Game's main group's activity&quot;. How is that <i>any </i>different from getting an Imbued Item?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I don't see how or why exclusive access to certain Mysteries denies the 'Games's main group's activity'. In fact, I would claim it <u><i>underlines</i></u>the need for cooperation to uncover secrets - after all, a Cabal exists so that they can uncover Supernal Mysteries, and why would you need others if you could do it all on your own? This is <u><i>exactly</i></u>the kind of mechanical system supporting/encouraging/requiring team cooperation that you claimed Beast was lacking, and praised in e.g. Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also: you don't need to include those very specific Mysteries, now do you? There are still plenty other options. You're literally getting stuck on an option, not the 'most basic game plot' to make it work. Plus as I tried to show above, there are plenty of ways to make it work, from a spot-lighting experience to make one player stand out for a while, to outright teamworking experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:17:30-07:00","id":1196797,"title":"","content":"I will lay other arguments for Mage as they are 'you can make it all your way as ST' - it's always true, but why other gamelines can be more cooperative and Mage is simply competing between players?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As long</b> <b>as seeing the Supernal Mystery that only one path can perceive isn't the <u>absolute</u> core or pinnacle of the story, there isn't a single problem with it from my point of view. </b><br /> And since you're the one creating the Mystery in the first place, that should be entirely in your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS the problem if I want to run story about Aedes or Ochemata, for example. And <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> are giving us needed Supernal Mysterie, that are connected to Supernal World - i.e. can be percived only by particular Path, until Summoned ( if there is possible for this Mystery ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, I don't see how or why exclusive access to certain Mysteries denies the 'Games's main group's activity'. In fact, I would claim it <u><i>underlines</i></u>the need for cooperation to uncover secrets - after all, a Cabal exists so that they can uncover Supernal Mysteries, and why would you need others if you could do it all on your own?</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Sharing Path's Mage Sight <b>does not</b> make you possible to solve other Path Mysteries without other mages.</u> YOU STILL needs other mages to cast their Path's Mage Sight - cause you only have your OWN Path Sight. So it's not 'I just solve all the Mysteries on my own' - cabal is still needed for you. Or at least good pals in your Orders - and with them it's the same as need to lend Imbued Items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: you don't need to include those very specific Mysteries, now do you? There are still plenty other options. You're literally getting stuck on an option, not the 'most basic game plot' to make it work. Plus as I tried to show above, there are plenty of ways to make it work, from a spot-lighting experience to make one player stand out for a while, to outright teamworking experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1196443#post1196443\">I <i>literally</i> started to write chronicle and it's Mystery that Aedes seems as perfect mechanical representation</a> - BEFORE all this debate. When game says what I do is clashing with idea for the game - before creation of sourcebook it will dwell in to - I try to point that problem before. As WHOLE <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> will be on Mysteries like Aedes. Without shared Path's Mage Sight - this book instead of being 'most useful supplement to be used' by me - becomes total waste then, if I cannot use stuff in it as plot devices for my groups.<br /> <br /> As to other games....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE your claims of Prometheans being simply able to make an Alchemical Pact, I am afraid that is wrong. Only Prometheans on the Path of Lead are capable of Branding a Throng. So yes, you DO need special powers. Or access to someone with those special powers. And Prometheans are rare...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here I stay slightly corrected - I mixed 1E rules with 2E<b> PtC</b> - my bad. But as you need in <b>Promethean</b> 2E Created with Refiment of Lead for it - and Prommies can rather easily change Refinement - it's still much 'free' than even Werewolf Sacred Hunt's. For Alchemical Pacts, all you need is a little time for character to switch Refinements, not even buying powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If every Werewolf can learn the Rite from the beginning, but effectively has to buy it, that doesn't make it free, now does it? It's a 2-dot rite, too. Someone within the group has to give up on a 2-dot Rite so the group can participate in the &quot;Game's main group's activity&quot;. How is that <i>any </i>different from getting an Imbued Item?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\">I was pointed by Werewolf devs that Sacred Hunt Rite is 'free' by this free dots given to characters on start. </a>It maybe is not really free, but cleary much more 'freeish' than hard ban of Path Sight sharing or even taking by characters Imbued Item Merit as needs ( werewolf characters have still all Merits to choose, and only some Rites they sacrifice. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196780#post1196780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is <u><i>exactly</i></u>the kind of mechanical system supporting/encouraging/requiring team cooperation that you claimed Beast was lacking, and praised in e.g. Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was claiming that <b>Beast</b> have a lot 1on1's scenes with sating Hungry - and I stay corrected, by you pointing me earlier in this topic that other players cooperation is encouraged inside brood in <b>BtP</b>. Just like would want to be in <b>Mage </b>in cabal...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-18-2018, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:25:49-07:00","id":1196847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I will lay other arguments for Mage as they are 'you can make it all your way as ST' - it's always true, but why other gamelines can be more cooperative and Mage is simply competing between players?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry, I do not see where the players are competing? If anything, they need to work <i>with </i>each other. They cooperate. Otherwise, they won't get the job done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It IS the problem if I want to run story about Aedes or Ochemata, for example. And <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> are giving us needed Supernal Mysterie, that are connected to Supernal World - i.e. can be percived only by particular Path, until Summoned ( if there is possible for this Mystery ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, in that case/ if it IS the absolute core of your chronicle, it is not as easy. You can still go with several different Aedes to be found, each attuned to one of the player's paths. Or the teamwork route mentioned above, where while only one player actively scrutinizes the mystery, the others get their spotlight in getting him there (think Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone: No Ron, no finale. No Hermione, no finale. Each one of those contributed just as much, if not more, to the group effort as Harry). Your players have to realize/understand they don't need every Cabal member to scrutinize every Mystery: if one of them manages to bring the knowledge to the rest, that's fine. What matters is that everyone gets involved and something meaningful to do.<br /> <br /> Don't knock the book before it's out, though. There can still be supernal mysteries that are not Path-exclusive in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Sharing Path's Mage Sight <b>does not</b> make you possible to solve other Path Mysteries without other mages.</u> YOU STILL needs other mages to cast their Path's Mage Sight - cause you only have your OWN Path Sight. So it's not 'I just solve all the Mysteries on my own' - cabal is still needed for you. Or at least good pals in your Orders - and with them it's the same as need to lend Imbued Items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm, okay? I never claimed that works? Also, that is what I considered a bonus - you <i>cannot </i>do things on your own, you need your Cabal/other mages.<br /> So... you agree with me? Sorry, I can't quite get what you're trying to say, because I read your lines as you disagreeing with me from a locutionary point, but agreeing with me in what is actually said. In case you're refering to this line: &quot;why would you need others if you could do it all on your own?&quot;, that was a rhethorical question.<br /> <br /> However, now I have this idea in my head where you need Moros-aligned Life-Sight to properly deal with the mystery, so the Moros of the team needs to borror Life Sight... Pretty sure that will be a fun puzzle to solve. Just need to make sure to drop the right hints...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1196443#post1196443\">I <i>literally</i> started to write chronicle and it's Mystery that Aedes seems as perfect mechanical representation</a> - BEFORE all this debate. When game says what I do is clashing with idea for the game - before creation of sourcebook it will dwell in to - I try to point that problem before. As WHOLE <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> will be on Mysteries like Aedes. Without shared Path's Mage Sight - this book instead of being 'most useful supplement to be used' by me - becomes total waste then, if I cannot use stuff in it as plot devices for my groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, then it is clashing with YOUR specific idea for a game. Most people apparently don't have a problem with it - this is what houserules are for: make the game suit your table.<br /> I see your problem, but this is territory that everyone has to deal with at some point; when they dealt with something in their games before new Sourcebooks came out, which addressed those topics in a different manner. You have to decide what to keep or throw out. Sometimes that sucks.<br /> And again, don't knock the book before it's out - Aedes are just one type of Supernal Mystery, no one said they're all like those. If you decide the book's not for you, that's okay - don't use it. No one will force you to. If you find interesting alternative approaches, put them on the forum, that's what the hubs are for. If you're unsure whether or not to buy it, do what many others do: wait for the first people to read through it, and give their opinions/reviews on the forum. Ask questions. Use that to get a better picture and decide for yourself.<br /> <br /> You could simply rule that everyone can see them as long as you have the necessary Arcana. However, that does make them less special, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to other games....<br /> Okay, here I stay slightly corrected - I mixed 1E rules with 2E<b> PtC</b> - my bad. But as you need in <b>Promethean</b> 2E Created with Refiment of Lead for it - and Prommies can rather easily change Refinement - it's still much 'free' than even Werewolf Sacred Hunt's. For Alchemical Pacts, all you need is a little time for character to switch Refinements, not even buying powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And Plumbum isn't a rare Refinement, so everyone gets access to it. You still need to pick special abilities, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\">I was pointed by Werewolf devs that Sacred Hunt Rite is 'free' by this free dots given to characters on start. </a>It maybe is not really free, but cleary much more 'freeish' than hard ban of Path Sight sharing or even taking by characters Imbued Item Merit as needs ( werewolf characters have still all Merits to choose, and only some Rites they sacrifice. )</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, because you don't necessarily need it to play, so my 'claim' you need it was uncalled for. I was getting controversial and apologize for that.<br /> I still don't think it's free. It's just obtainable with the starting resources. And well worth the price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196797#post1196797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was claiming that <b>Beast</b> have a lot 1on1's scenes with sating Hungry - and I stay corrected, by you pointing me earlier in this topic that other players cooperation is encouraged inside brood in <b>BtP</b>. Just like would want to be in <b>Mage </b>in cabal...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is <i>exactly </i>what the Aedes do: encourage player cooperation by forcing them to rely on each other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:50:26-07:00","id":1196852,"title":"","content":"Finally agreeing with mostly what you talk. Only this thing...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196847#post1196847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is <i>exactly </i>what the Aedes do: encourage player cooperation by forcing them to rely on each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>it's</i> <i>not cooperation</i>. It's 'ST takes one player out of game group, do some rolls with him, players cast some spells - ST is doing elaborate description only for one player - and then they two return to the players group'. It's literally been few session of 2E <b>Mage</b> of mine two previous chronicles! And it's a basic of problem - other players are not included if you do 'deep' Mage Sight scene, where one player get's all the Supernal glory details and interactions with it. And it's OFTEN in gameplay - like 1/3rd of all scenes in typical Mage session.<br /> <br /> Even <b>Beast</b> do not have this kind problem with Sating the Hunger - brood will <i>help you</i> prepare Sating so they will get Family Dinner by watching and sometimes intervening in your Sating ( for example, if victim is trying to run away ). In <b>Mage,</b> Mage Sight scene is 'ST is running everything with only one player'. It's bad for party and gameplay dynamics.<br /> <br /> And this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196847#post1196847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you decide the book's not for you, that's okay - don't use it. No one will force you to.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Signs of Sorcery</b> sounds like <b>Mage</b> 2E version of <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> - i.e. unofficial 2nd part of 2E corebook. From the material pointed in previews - it will be the same game changer like the <b>Beast Players Guide</b>. And I'm really <i>hungry</i> for the stuff shown in the book previews.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not the problem with the stuff in <b>SoS</b> I have problem - i<b>t's a LACK of cooperative investigation in the Mage-2E-as-the-game itself.</b> Supernal Mysteries in <b>SoS</b> are just examples of the stuff that will be problem. I can made my own Supernal Mysteries for the game - it does not change the fact that not sharing Mage Sight between Paths leads to 1/5th of the group to interact with them, by the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:11:25-07:00","id":1196873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196852#post1196852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally agreeing with mostly what you talk. Only this thing...<br /> <br /> <br /> No, <i>it's</i> <i>not cooperation</i>. It's 'ST takes one player out of game group, do some rolls with him, players cast some spells - ST is doing elaborate description only for one player - and then they two return to the players group'. It's literally been few session of 2E <b>Mage</b> of mine two previous chronicles! And it's a basic of problem - other players are not included if you do 'deep' Mage Sight scene, where one player get's all the Supernal glory details and interactions with it. And it's OFTEN in gameplay - like 1/3rd of all scenes in typical Mage session.<br /> <br /> Even <b>Beast</b> do not have this kind problem with Sating the Hunger - brood will <i>help you</i> prepare Sating so they will get Family Dinner by watching and sometimes intervening in your Sating ( for example, if victim is trying to run away ). In <b>Mage,</b> Mage Sight scene is 'ST is running everything with only one player'. It's bad for party and gameplay dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... is not how it usually plays out for me? Sounds like you need to rethink your approach with these concepts, honestly. Why don't you let the others hear the elaborate description? They should be able to seperate IC and OOC knowledge like that. Also, this is still not competition of players, imo. But nevermind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190520-2e-solo-focused-cod-gamelines?p=1196852#post1196852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> sounds like <b>Mage</b> 2E version of <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> - i.e. unofficial 2nd part of 2E corebook. From the material pointed in previews - it will be the same game changer like the <b>Beast Players Guide</b>. And I'm really <i>hungry</i> for the stuff shown in the book previews.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not the problem with the stuff in <b>SoS</b> I have problem - i<b>t's a LACK of cooperative investigation in the Mage-2E-as-the-game itself.</b> Supernal Mysteries in <b>SoS</b> are just examples of the stuff that will be problem. I can made my own Supernal Mysteries for the game - it does not change the fact that not sharing Mage Sight between Paths leads to 1/5th of the group to interact with them, by the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pointed towards you not having to use it because of your claim that &quot;Without shared Path's Mage Sight - this book instead of being 'most useful supplement to be used' by me - becomes total waste then, if I cannot use stuff in it as plot devices for my groups.&quot;<br /> <br /> I still disagree, but after repeatedly trying to explain my point of view/understanding your point of view, as well as reading some of your other threads, I think we'll just have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}